////////////////////////////
// SheepFarm (register-only) properties
//
// Express the bug and the fix:
// - Bug: register does not write timestamp, so timestamp stays 0 and user can register again.
// - Fix (target semantics): after one register, timestamp becomes non-zero, and any further
//   recv_register by same msgSender becomes invalid.
////////////////////////////

// If the caller already has a non-zero timestamp, a new registration is invalid.
// This induces the guard `t == 0` for the synthesized register rule.
invalidTx() :-
  recv_register(_),
  msgSender(user),
  villageTimestamp(user, t),
  t != 0.

